                                "sense_id": "b1d83f87-1d38-354d-8911-320d848ca672",
                                "text": "A woman at the next table, behind Guild, was saying oratorically: “I can always tell when I'm getting swacked because the skin gets tight across my forehead, but it don't ever do me any good because by that time I'm too swacked to care whether I'm getting swacked or not.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0abebad-6e97-4870-9fff-688d557936a2",
                                "sense_id": "b1d83f87-1d38-354d-8911-320d848ca672",
                                "text": "\"Look what we've got.\" Mitch brought out a bottle of pink champagne. \"I'll get swacked if I drink before I eat,\" Sonia said."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea8673b7-ec9b-4045-9a1b-3c5828e37191",
                                "sense_id": "b1d83f87-1d38-354d-8911-320d848ca672",
                                "text": "It was nearly dusk when Wallace, swacked on power and assorted chemicals, staggered out of the Hilton Inn parking lot to his rental car."
                            }
